# Rover 14 P2 four-door saloon, 1934-1948.
#
# The Rover Fourteen of the P2 generation: 4,191 mm long, 1,575 mm wide, 1,651 mm
# high, 2,692 mm wheelbase; 1,901 cc six. The six-cylinder P2 was the upper-middle
# Rover before and after the war. https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Rover_P2
#
# Colours: Black, Green, Maroon and Grey are documented Rover finishes of the
# period.
#
# Weight: 25 in total (black 9, green 7, maroon 5, grey 4).
#
# Speed 115 km/h; comfort 65/428 (line). Classes 2,3,4.
# Dates: 1934-1948 with a road tail to about 1965.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/rover-14-p2.blend. References:
# citycars/references/rover-14-p2/ (gitignored). Images via Wikimedia Commons.

obj=citycar
name=Rover14P2(Black)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=9
intro_year=1934
intro_month=10
retire_year=1965
retire_month=6
speed=115
class=2,3,4
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=65
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=428

